WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.020 line:6% position:50% align:center
Production and handoff: a simulated client project, parts four and five of five.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.160 line:6% position:50% align:center
The eval harness found real gaps.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.460 line:6% position:50% align:center
Spanish questions were blocked before they reached the model.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.900 line:6% position:50% align:center
Now the answer comes back in Spanish, from the English documents, with its source.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.700 line:6% position:50% align:center
Emergencies in other words, or in Spanish, were missed.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.310 line:6% position:50% align:center
Now they get the safety message at once, with no model call.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.880 line:6% position:50% align:center
A guest booked at the Mountain Lodge wrote to the Beach Resort.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.290 line:6% position:50% align:center
The agent used to answer for the wrong hotel.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.150 line:6% position:50% align:center
Now the booking is looked up first, so the reply is about the right one.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:42.380 line:6% position:50% align:center
On a local copy, the owner's Operations page shows requests, latency and cost against budgets.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:48.300 line:6% position:50% align:center
Every log record has personal data removed before it is stored, and is kept for thirty days.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:01:01.540 line:6% position:50% align:center
And the handoff package: runbooks, service levels, staff guides, and a daily health check that knows a sleeping free app from a broken one.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.220 line:6% position:50% align:center
Every number comes from a saved run.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.730 line:6% position:50% align:center
The links are on screen.
